+# Credit notes for issued invoices (#66)
+
+Support currently refunds customers by hand and finance reconciles the
+refunds in a spreadsheet. This adds credit notes to `Invoice`.
+
+## What changes
+
+- `Invoice.creditNote(number, issuedOn, reason, items)` refunds whole units of
+  one or more invoice lines. Each unit is credited at the price, discount and
+  tax rate it was invoiced at, so crediting a line in full returns exactly what
+  the customer was charged for it.
+- Credit notes can be raised against `issued` or `paid` invoices, need a
+  reason, cannot predate the invoice, and cannot credit more units of a line
+  than were invoiced (across all notes).
+- Refunds are money going back to the customer, so the total credited can
+  never exceed what the customer has paid.
+- New `creditNotes` and `amountCredited` getters. Credit notes do not change
+  the invoice status or `balance` (a refunded invoice stays `paid`; reporting
+  reads `amountCredited`).
+
+## Testing
+
+New `tests/invoice-credit-notes.test.ts`.
